# Alt 3 — Badged avatar (merged identity)

**One avatar carries both identities.** The user avatar wears a small org badge in its lower-right corner — the way Slack stamps a workspace on your face, or a notification dot. A single row, single menu. The org is *shown* at rest (the badge) but only *switched* inside the menu.

### Resting

```
├───────────────────────────────┤
│ ╭───────────────────────────╮ │
│ │  ╭───╮                    │ │
│ │  │GD │   Greg Daniels  ⌄ │ │
│ │  ╰──╴▢   Acme Inc         │ │
│ ╰───────────────────────────╯ │
└───────────────────────────────┘
       the ▢ org badge tucks onto the
        avatar's lower-right corner
```

### Clicked (one menu, both sections)

```
   ╭─────────────────────────────╮
   │  ✓ ▢ Acme Inc               │
   │    ▢ Globex Corp            │
   │  + New organization         │
   ├─────────────────────────────┤
   │  ⚙  Settings                │
   │  ↗  Sign out                │
   ╰─────────────────────────────╯
┌───────────────────────────────┐
│ (GD)▢ Greg Daniels        ⌃  │
│      Acme Inc                 │
└───────────────────────────────┘
```

### Collapsed sidebar
The badged avatar reads cleanly even tiny — org context survives the collapse.

```
│(GD)│
│  ▢ │
```

**Pros:** one glyph encodes both identities; org context always visible without a full row; works great collapsed.
**Cons:** the badge is small — fine for an icon/color org identity, weak if orgs are only distinguished by long names; needs real org icons to shine (you now have concept/field icons, so plausible).
